<p>On the basis of exchange rates from 7-10  February, the RMG for the pound is above +5 per cent, at 6.495 per cent. Therefore the UK green rate is currently forecast to enter its second confirmation period on 17 February. The RMG for the Irish punt is also over + 5 per cent, at +5.656 per cent. It is therefore also forecast to enter a second confirmation period on 17 February. If both currencies maintain their current strength they will revalue on 29 March. All currencies with negative average RMGs at the end of the period will be devalued by reducing their RMGs to zero. Hence, devaluations are currently forecast for the Spanish peseta and Belgian franc on 17 February. During confirmation periods the 3-day (6 per cent) rule is suspended.</p>
